  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="ac7b-72f5-82f9-23d6" name="Militia Cavalry Mount" publicationId="48c2-d023-0069-001a" page="37" hidden="false">
      <description>A model with a Militia cavalry mount that chooses to Run gains the Shrouded (5+) special rule until the start of the controlling player’s next turn.


A model with the Infantry Unit Type that selects a Militia cavalry mount as an upgrade must change its Unit Type to Cavalry, keeping any Unit Sub-types it previously had.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="e626-c3b1-e724-c6fc" name="Provenance" hidden="false">
      <description>Provenance</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="976f-9e14-413c-5bea" name="Emplaced" publicationId="48c2-d023-0069-001a" page="24" hidden="false">
      <description>A unit that includes any models with this special rule may only make the Return Fire or Overwatch Core Reactions or the Interceptor Advanced Reaction – no other Reaction of any kind may be made. Additionally, if forced to Fall Back for any reason, all models in the unit are immediately removed as casualties.

If taken as part of a Mortalis Assault Force Organisation Chart, a unit that includes any models with this Special Rule may only make the Suppress Reaction.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Invulnerable Save (X)" id="f955-4cfa-2eff-1923" hidden="false">
      <description>The model has an Invulnerable Save of X, which may be taken against any Wound instead of its armour save.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Household Retinue" id="3d09-eaf4-fba4-ec20" hidden="false">
      <description>Listed on this datasheet but not defined in the conversion doc.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
